# LIKWID-only PMU (Intel + AMD EPYC)

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**.

## Law

- **Intel** (`host_cpu_hw` on SKX/CLX/ICX/SPR/EMR/GNR/SRF) and **EPYC** Rome/Milan/Genoa/Turin core + DF + RAPL go through **LIKWID** only.
- If LIKWID init/setup fails, **disable** `host_cpu_hw` (and DF on EPYC) — **no MSR fallback**, no `fallback_fill`, no `msr_io` core PMC path.
- Do **not** reintroduce `intel_x86_pmc_gpr4` / `intel_x86_pmc_gpr8`, `intel_4pmc3` / `intel_8pmc3`, `msr_io`, or AMD `amd64_pmc` / native MSR `amd64_df` / emit `amd_x86_pmc` or bare `amd_x86_uncore_df`.
- DF `st_name`s are family-named: `amd_x86_uncore_df_{rome,milan,genoa,turin}` (IMC pattern).
- CPUID allowlists for EPYC are **server model ranges** only (`amd_cpuid_match.c`).
- **Runtime begin order:** `stats_runtime.c` begins `host_cpu_hw` before other types so LIKWID `HPMinit` runs before AMD DF/RAPL begin. Registry table order stays `st_name` sorted for binary search.
- **`amd_x86_rapl` begin** must require `cpu_counter_metrics_likwid_ready()` (same gate as DF). Flat RAPL `0 0` rows are a **failure mode**, not healthy idle — disable the type when LIKWID never initialized.
- **Begin failures must be journal-visible:** `likwid_backend_begin` and `likwid_pmc_adapter_setup_events` log which step failed (`HPMinit` / `addEventSet` / `setupCounters` / `startCounters`) and the event string; do not rely on quiet stderr redirect alone. On quiet setup failure, retry the failing LIKWID call once with stderr restored so “PMC in use” / force hints reach the journal.
- **`LIKWID_FORCE` default:** `likwid_pmc_adapter_init` calls `likwid_pmc_adapter_ensure_force_env()` (`setenv("LIKWID_FORCE","1",0)`) so in-use core PMCs can be claimed (C-API equivalent of `likwid-perfctr -f`). Operators may opt out with `LIKWID_FORCE=0` before start.
- **RAPL MSR path is runtime:** `likwid_rapl_collect_path()` / `likwid_rapl_collect_socket_mj` select AMD vs Intel MSRs from `processor` (EPYC → AMD). Do **not** gate RAPL `power_read` on `MONITOR_ARCH_*`. An Intel-`MONITOR_ARCH` binary on Turin that still used `collect_intel_socket_mj` SEGVs in `power_read` (amd-rtx live residual).
- **Live amd-rtx healthy bar:** unit `active` (not core-dump restart loop), shm sample age &lt; 300s, `@full` has `host_cpu_hw` + `amd_x86_uncore_df_turin` + non-flat `amd_x86_rapl`. `rpm_debug_shm_verify` refuses validate when the service is not active after install.
- **AMD core eventset:** use `LS_DISPATCH_ALL` (not bare `LS_DISPATCH`) — LIKWID Zen tables only define `LS_DISPATCH_*` umasks.

See [LIKWID_MIGRATION.md](../LIKWID_MIGRATION.md).

